ence.com/w/cpp/utility/compare/named_comparison_functions.html \"cpp/utility/compare/named comparison functions\")<br>(C++20)(C++20)(C++20)`` | | |     |\n| --- |\n| [is\\_neqis\\_gtis\\_gteq](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/compare/named_comparison_functions.html \"cpp/utility/compare/named comparison functions\")<br>(C++20)(C++20)(C++20) | | |\n|  | | |     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n| General utilities |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| [Function objects](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/functional.html \"cpp/utility/functional\") |\n| [Bit manipulation](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/bit.html \"cpp/utility/bit\")(C++20) |\n| [C-style bit manipulation](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/utility/stdbit&action=edit&redlink=1 \"cpp/utility/stdbit (page does not exist)\")(C++26) |\n| [bitset](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/bitset.html \"cpp/utility/bitset\") |\n| [hash](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/hash.html \"cpp/utility/hash\")<br>(C++11) | |\n| [Relational operators](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility.html#Relational_operators \"cpp/utility\")(deprecated in C++20) |\n| |     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| [rel\\_ops::operator!=rel\\_ops::operator>](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/rel_ops/operator_cmp.html \"cpp/utility/rel ops/operator cmp\")<br>`` | | |     |\n| --- |\n| [rel\\_ops::operator<=rel\\_ops::operator>=](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/rel_ops/operator_cmp.html \"cpp/utility/rel ops/operator cmp\") | |\n| [Integer comparison functions](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility.html#Integer_comparison_functions \"cpp/utility\") |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| [cmp\\_equalcmp\\_lesscmp\\_less\\_than](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/intcmp.html \"cpp/utility/intcmp\")<br>(C++20)(C++20)(C++20)`` | | |     |\n| --- |\n| [cmp\\_not\\_equalcmp\\_greatercmp\\_greater\\_than](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/intcmp.html \"cpp/utility/intcmp\")<br>(C++20)(C++20)(C++20) | |\n| [in\\_range](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/in_range.html \"cpp/utility/in range\")<br>(C++20) |\n| [Swap](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility.html#Swap \"cpp/utility\") and [type operations](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility.html#Type_operations \"cpp/utility\") |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| [swap](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/swap.html \"cpp/algorithm/swap\") |\n| [ranges::swap](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/ranges/swap.html \"cpp/utility/ranges/swap\")<br>(C++20) |\n| [exchange](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/exchange.html \"cpp/utility/exchange\")<br>(C++14) |\n| [declval](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/declval.html \"cpp/utility/declval\")<br>(C++11) |\n| [to\\_underlying](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/to_underlying.html \"cpp/utility/to underlying\")<br>(C++23) | | |     |\n| --- |\n| [forward](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/forward.html \"cpp/utility/forward\")<br>(C++11) |\n| [forward\\_like](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/forward_like.html \"cpp/utility/forward like\")<br>(C++23) |\n| [move](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/move.html \"cpp/utility/move\")<br>(C++11) |\n| [move\\_if\\_noexcept](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/move_if_noexcept.html \"cpp/utility/move if noexcept\")<br>(C++11) |\n| [as\\_const](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/as_const.html \"cpp/utility/as const\")<br>(C++17) | |\n| Common vocabulary types |\n| |     |\n| --- |\n| [pair](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/pair.html \"cpp/utility/pair\") |\n| [tuple](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/tuple.html \"cpp/utility/tuple\")<br>(C++11) |\n| **optional**<br>(C++17) |\n| [any](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/any.html \"cpp/utility/any\")<br>(C++17) |\n| [variant](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/variant.html \"cpp/utility/variant\")<br>(C++17) | | |     |\n| --- |\n| [tuple\\_size](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/tuple_size.html \"cpp/utility/tuple size\")<br>(C++11) |\n| [tuple\\_element](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/tuple_element.html \"cpp/utility/tuple element\")<br>(C++11) |\n| [apply](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/apply.html \"cpp/utility/apply\")<br>(C++17) |\n| [make\\_from\\_tuple](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/make_from_tuple.html \"cpp/utility/make from tuple\")<br>(C++17) |\n| [expected](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/expected.html \"cpp/utility/expected\")<br>(C++23) | |\n|  |\n|  | | |\n\n[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/utility/navbar_content&action=edit)\n\n**`std::optional`**\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| [Member functions](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional.html#Member_functions \"cpp/utility/optional\") |\n| [optional::optional](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/optional.html \"cpp/utility/optional/optional\") |\n| [optional::~optional](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/~optional.html \"cpp/utility/optional/~optional\") |\n| [optional::operator=](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/operator=.html \"cpp/utility/optional/operator=\") |\n| [Observers](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional.html#Observers \"cpp/utility/optional\") |\n| [optional::operator->optional::operator\\*](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/operator%252A.html \"cpp/utility/optional/operator*\") |\n| [optional::operator booloptional::has\\_value](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/operator_bool.html \"cpp/utility/optional/operator bool\") |\n| [optional::value](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/value.html \"cpp/utility/optional/value\") |\n| [optional::value\\_or](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/value_or.html \"cpp/utility/optional/value or\") |\n| [Iterators](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional.html#Iterators \"cpp/utility/optional\") |\n| [optional::begin](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/begin.html \"cpp/utility/optional/begin\")<br>(C++26) |\n| [optional::end](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/end.html \"cpp/utility/optional/end\")<br>(C++26) |\n| [Monadic operations](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional.html#Monadic_operations \"cpp/utility/optional\") |\n| [optional::and\\_then](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/and_then.html \"cpp/utility/optional/and then\")<br>(C++23) |\n| [optional::transform](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/transform.html \"cpp/utility/optional/transform\")<br>(C++23) |\n| [optional::or\\_else](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/or_else.html \"cpp/utility/optional/or else\")<br>(C++23) |\n| [Modifiers](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional.html#Modifiers \"cpp/utility/optional\") |\n| [optional::emplace](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/emplace.html \"cpp/utility/optional/emplace\") |\n| [optional::swap](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/swap.html \"cpp/utility/optional/swap\") |\n| [optional::reset](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/reset.html \"cpp/utility/optional/reset\") |\n| [Non-member functions](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional.html#Non-member_functions \"cpp/utility/optional\") |\n| [operator==operator!=operator<operator<=operator>operator>=operator<=>](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/operator_cmp.html \"cpp/utility/optional/operator cmp\")<br>(C++20) |\n| [make\\_optional](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/make_optional.html \"cpp/utility/optional/make optional\") |\n| [swap(std::optional)](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/swap2.html \"cpp/utility/optional/swap2\") |\n| [Deduction guides](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/deduction_guides.html \"cpp/utility/optional/deduction guides\") |\n| [Helper classes](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional.html#Helper_classes \"cpp/utility/optional\") |\n| [hash<std::optional>](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/hash.html \"cpp/utility/optional/hash\") |\n| [nullopt\\_t](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/nullopt_t.html \"cpp/utility/optional/nullopt t\") |\n| [in\\_place\\_t](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/in_place.html \"cpp/utility/in place\") |\n| [bad\\_optional\\_access](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/bad_optional_access.html \"cpp/utility/optional/bad optional access\") |\n| [Helper objects](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional.html#Helpers \"cpp/utility/optional\") |\n| [nullopt](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/nullopt.html \"cpp/utility/optional/nullopt\") |\n| [in\\_place](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/in_place.html \"cpp/utility/in place\") |\n\n[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/utility/optional/navbar_content&action=edit)\n\n|     |     |     |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Defined in header `<optional>` |  |  |\n| template<class T ><br>class optional; |  | (since C++17) |\n|  |  |  |\n\nThe class template `std::optional` manages an optional contained value, i.e. a value that may or may not be present.\n\nA common use case for `optional` is the return value of a function that may fail. As opposed to other approaches, such as [std::pair](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/pair.html) <T, bool>, `optional` handles expensive-to-construct objects well and is more readable, as the intent is expressed explicitly.\n\nAny instance of `optional` at any given point in time either _contains a value_ or _does not contain a value_.\n\nIf an `optional` contains a value, the value is guaranteed to be [nested within](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/objects.html#Address \"cpp/language/object\") the `optional` object. Thus, an `optional` object models an object, not a pointer, even though [operator\\*()](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/operator%252A.html \"cpp/utility/optional/operator*\") and [operator->()](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/operator%252A.html \"cpp/utility/optional/operator*\") are defined.\n\nWhen an object of type `optional<T>` is [contextually converted to bool](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/implicit_cast.html#Contextual_conversions \"cpp/language/implicit conversion\"), the conversion returns true if the object contains a value and false if it does not contain a value.\n\nThe `optional` object contains a value in the following conditions:\n\n- The object is initialized with/assigned from a value of type `T` or another `optional` that contains a value.\n\n\nThe object does not contain a value in the following conditions:\n\n- The object is default-initialized.\n\n- The object is initialized with/assigned from a value of type [std::nullopt\\_t](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/nullopt_t.html \"cpp/utility/optional/nullopt t\") or an `optional` object that does not contain a value.\n\n- The member function [reset()](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/reset.html \"cpp/utility/optional/reset\") is called.\n\n\n|     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n| The `optional` object is a [`view`](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/ranges/view.html \"cpp/ranges/view\") that contains either one element if it _contains a value_, or otherwise zero elements if it does not contain a value. The lifetime of the contained element is bound to the object. | (since C++26) |\n\nThere are no optional references, functions, arrays, or (possibly cv-qualified) void; a program is ill-formed if it instantiates an `optional` with such a type. In addition, a program is ill-formed if it instantiates an `optional` with the (possibly cv-qualified) tag types [std::nullopt\\_t](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/nullopt_t.html \"cpp/utility/optional/nullopt t\") or [std::in\\_place\\_t](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/in_place.html \"cpp/utility/in place\").\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| ## Contents<br>- [1Template parameters](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional.html#Template_parameters)<br>- [2Nested types](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional.html#Nested_types)<br>- [3Data members](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional.html#Data_members)<br>- [4Member functions](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional.html#Member_functions)<br>  - [4.1Iterators](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional.html#Iterators)<br>  - [4.2Observers](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional.html#Observers)<br>  - [4.3Monadic operations](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional.html#Monadic_operations)<br>  - [4.4Modifiers](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional.html#Modifiers)<br>- [5Non-member functions](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional.html#Non-member_functions)<br>- [6Helper classes](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional.html#Helper_classes)<br>- [7Helpers](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional.html#Helpers)<br>- [8Helper specializations](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional.html#Helper_specializations)<br>- [9Deduction guides](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional.html#Deduction_guides)<br>- [10Notes](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional.html#Notes)<br>- [11Example](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional.html#Example)<br>- [12Defect reports](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional.html#Defect_reports)<br>- [13See also](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional.html#See_also) |\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/utility/optional&action=edit&section=1 \"Edit section: Template parameters\")\\]Template parameters\n\n|     |     |     |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| T | - | the type of the value to manage initialization state for. The type must meet the requirements of [Destructible](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/Destructible.html \"cpp/named req/Destructible\") (in particular, array and reference types are not allowed). |\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/utility/optional&action=edit&section=2 \"Edit section: Nested types\")\\]Nested types\n\n|     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n| Type | Definition |\n| `value_type` | `T` |\n| `iterator`(since C++26) | implementation-defined [LegacyRandomAccessIterator](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/RandomAccessIterator.html \"cpp/named req/RandomAccessIterator\"), [ConstexprIterator](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/ConstexprIterator.html \"cpp/named req/ConstexprIterator\"), and [`contiguous_iterator`](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/iterator/contiguous_iterator.html \"cpp/iterator/contiguous iterator\") whose `value_type` and `reference` are [std::remove\\_cv\\_t](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/remove_cv.html) <T> and T&, respectively. |\n| `const_iterator`(since C++26) | implementation-defined [LegacyRandomAccessIterator](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/RandomAccessIterator.html \"cpp/named req/RandomAccessIterator\"), [ConstexprIterator](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/ConstexprIterator.html \"cpp/named req/ConstexprIterator\"), and [`contiguous_iterator`](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/iterator/contiguous_iterator.html \"cpp/iterator/contiguous iterator\") whose `value_type` and `reference` are [std::remove\\_cv\\_t](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/types/remove_cv.html) <T> and const T&, respectively. |\n\nAll requirements on the iterator types of a [Container](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/Container.html \"cpp/named req/Container\") apply to the `iterator` type of `optional` as well.\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/utility/optional&action=edit&section=3 \"Edit section: Data members\")\\]Data members\n\n|     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n| `T*``val` | a pointer to the contained object (if exists)<br>(exposition-only member object\\*) |\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/utility/optional&action=edit&section=4 \"Edit section: Member functions\")\\]Member functions\n\n|     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n| [(constructor)](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/optional.html \"cpp/utility/optional/optional\") | constructs the `optional` object <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/utility/optional/dsc_constructor&action=edit) |\n| [(destructor)](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/~optional.html \"cpp/utility/optional/~optional\") | destroys the contained value, if there is one <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/utility/optional/dsc_destructor&action=edit) |\n| [operator=](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/operator=.html \"cpp/utility/optional/operator=\") | assigns contents <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/utility/optional/dsc_operator%3D&action=edit) |\n| ##### Iterators |\n| [begin](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/begin.html \"cpp/utility/optional/begin\")<br>(C++26) | returns an iterator to the beginning <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/utility/optional/dsc_begin&action=edit) |\n| [end](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/end.html \"cpp/utility/optional/end\")<br>(C++26) | returns an iterator to the end <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/utility/optional/dsc_end&action=edit) |\n| ##### Observers |\n| [operator->operator\\*](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/operator%252A.html \"cpp/utility/optional/operator*\") | accesses the contained value <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/utility/optional/dsc_operator*&action=edit) |\n| [operator boolhas\\_value](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/operator_bool.html \"cpp/utility/optional/operator bool\") | checks whether the object contains a value <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/utility/optional/dsc_operator_bool&action=edit) |\n| [value](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/value.html \"cpp/utility/optional/value\") | returns the contained value <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/utility/optional/dsc_value&action=edit) |\n| [value\\_or](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/value_or.html \"cpp/utility/optional/value or\") | returns the contained value if available, another value otherwise <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/utility/optional/dsc_value_or&action=edit) |\n| ##### Monadic operations |\n| [and\\_then](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/and_then.html \"cpp/utility/optional/and then\")<br>(C++23) | returns the result of the given function on the contained value if it exists, or an empty `optional` otherwise <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/utility/optional/dsc_and_then&action=edit) |\n| [transform](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/transform.html \"cpp/utility/optional/transform\")<br>(C++23) | returns an `optional` containing the transformed contained value if it exists, or an empty `optional` otherwise <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/utility/optional/dsc_transform&action=edit) |\n| [or\\_else](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/or_else.html \"cpp/utility/optional/or else\")<br>(C++23) | returns the `optional` itself if it contains a value, or the result of the given function otherwise <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/utility/optional/dsc_or_else&action=edit) |\n| ##### Modifiers |\n| [swap](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/swap.html \"cpp/utility/optional/swap\") | exchanges the contents <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/utility/optional/dsc_swap&action=edit) |\n| [reset](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/reset.html \"cpp/utility/optional/reset\") | destroys any contained value <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/utility/optional/dsc_reset&action=edit) |\n| [emplace](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/emplace.html \"cpp/utility/optional/emplace\") | constructs the contained value in-place <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/utility/optional/dsc_emplace&action=edit) |\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/utility/optional&action=edit&section=5 \"Edit section: Non-member functions\")\\]Non-member functions\n\n|     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n| [operator==operator!=operator<operator<=operator>operator>=operator<=>](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/operator_cmp.html \"cpp/utility/optional/operator cmp\")<br>(C++17)(C++17)(C++17)(C++17)(C++17)(C++17)(C++20) | compares `optional` objects <br>(function template)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/utility/optional/dsc_operator_cmp&action=edit) |\n| [make\\_optional](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/make_optional.html \"cpp/utility/optional/make optional\")<br>(C++17) | creates an `optional` object <br>(function template)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/utility/optional/dsc_make_optional&action=edit) |\n| [std::swap(std::optional)](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/swap2.html \"cpp/utility/optional/swap2\")<br>(C++17) | specializes the [std::swap](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/swap.html \"cpp/algorithm/swap\") algorithm <br>(function template)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/utility/optional/dsc_swap2&action=edit) |\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/utility/optional&action=edit&section=6 \"Edit section: Helper classes\")\\]Helper classes\n\n|     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n| [std::hash<std::optional>](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/hash.html \"cpp/utility/optional/hash\")<br>(C++17) | hash support for **`std::optional`**<br>(class template specialization)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/utility/optional/dsc_hash&action=edit) |\n| [nullopt\\_t](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/nullopt_t.html \"cpp/utility/optional/nullopt t\")<br>(C++17) | indicator of an `std::optional` that does not contain a value <br>(class)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/utility/optional/dsc_nullopt_t&action=edit) |\n| [bad\\_optional\\_access](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/bad_optional_access.html \"cpp/utility/optional/bad optional access\")<br>(C++17) | exception indicating checked access to an optional that doesn't contain a value <br>(class)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/utility/optional/dsc_bad_optional_access&action=edit) |\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/utility/optional&action=edit&section=7 \"Edit section: Helpers\")\\]Helpers\n\n|     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n| [nullopt](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/nullopt.html \"cpp/utility/optional/nullopt\")<br>(C++17) | an object of type `nullopt_t`<br>(constant)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/utility/optional/dsc_nullopt&action=edit) |\n| [in\\_placein\\_place\\_typein\\_place\\_indexin\\_place\\_tin\\_place\\_type\\_tin\\_place\\_index\\_t](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/in_place.html \"cpp/utility/in place\")<br>(C++17) | in-place construction tag<br>(tag)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/utility/optional/dsc_in_place&action=edit) |\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/utility/optional&action=edit&section=8 \"Edit section: Helper specializations\")\\]Helper specializations\n\n|     |     |     |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| template<class T ><br>constexprbool [ranges::enable\\_view](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/ranges/view.html) <std::optional<T>>=true; |  | (since C++26) |\n|  |  |  |\n\nThis specialization of [ranges::enable\\_view](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/ranges/view.html \"cpp/ranges/view\") makes `optional` satisfy [`view`](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/ranges/view.html \"cpp/ranges/view\").\n\n|     |     |     |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| template<class T ><br>constexprauto format\\_kind<std::optional<T>>= range\\_format::disabled; |  | (since C++26) |\n|  |  |  |\n\nThis specialization of format\\_kind disables the [range formatting support](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/format/ranges_formatter.html \"cpp/utility/format/ranges formatter\") of `optional`.\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/utility/optional&action=edit&section=9 \"Edit section: Deduction guides\")\\][Deduction guides](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional/deduction_guides.html \"cpp/utility/optional/deduction guides\")\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/utility/optional&action=edit&section=10 \"Edit section: Notes\")\\]Notes\n\n| [Feature-test](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/feature_test.html \"cpp/utility/feature test\") macro | Value | Std | Feature |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| [`__cpp_lib_optional`](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/experimental/feature_test.html#cpp_lib_optional \"cpp/feature test\") | [`201606L`](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/compiler_support/17.html#cpp_lib_optional_201606L \"cpp/compiler support/17\") | (C++17) | `std::optional` |\n| [`202106L`](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/compiler_support/23.html#cpp_lib_optional_202106L \"cpp/compiler support/23\") | (C++23)<br>(DR20) | Fully constexpr |\n| [`202110L`](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/compiler_support/23.html#cpp_lib_optional_202110L \"cpp/compiler support/23\") | (C++23) | [Monadic operations](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional.html#Monadic_operations) |\n| [`__cpp_lib_optional_range_support`](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/experimental/feature_test.html#cpp_lib_optional_range_support \"cpp/feature test\") | [`202406L`](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/compiler_support/26.html#cpp_lib_optional_range_support_202406L \"cpp/compiler support/26\") | (C++26) | Range support for `std::optional` |\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/utility/optional&action=edit&section=11 \"Edit section: Example\")\\]Example\n\nRun this code\n\n```\n#include <iostream>\n#include <optional>\n#include <string>\n\n// optional can be used as the return type of a factory that may fail\nstd::optional<std::string> create(bool b)\n{\n    if (b)\n        return \"Godzilla\";\n    return {};\n}\n\n// std::nullopt can be used to create any (empty) std::optional\nauto create2(bool b)\n{\n    return b ? std::optional<std::string>{\"Godzilla\"} : std::nullopt;\n}\n\nint main()\n{\n    std::cout << \"create(false) returned \"\n              << create(false).value_or(\"empty\") << '\\n';\n\n    // optional-returning factory functions are usable as conditions of while and if\n    if (auto str = create2(true))\n        std::cout << \"create2(true) returned \" << *str << '\\n';\n}\n```\n\nOutput:\n\n```\ncreate(false) returned empty\ncreate2(true) returned Godzilla\n```\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/utility/optional&action=edit&section=12 \"Edit section: Defect reports\")\\]Defect reports\n\nThe following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n\n| DR | Applied to | Behavior as published | Correct behavior |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| [LWG 4141](https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue4141) | C++17 | the requirement of storage<br>allocation was confusing | the contained object must be<br>nested within the `optional` object |\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/utility/optional&action=edit&section=13 \"Edit section: See also\")\\]See also\n\n|     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n| [variant](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/variant.html \"cpp/utility/variant\")<br>(C++17) | a type-safe discriminated union <br>(class template)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/utility/dsc_variant&action=edit) |\n| [any](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/any.html \"cpp/utility/any\")<br>(C++17) | objects that hold instances of any [CopyConstructible](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/CopyConstructible.html \"cpp/named req/CopyConstructible\") type <br>(class)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/utility/dsc_any&action=edit) |\n| [expected](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/expected.html \"cpp/utility/expected\")<br>(C++23) | a wrapper that contains either an expected or error value <br>(class template)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/utility/dsc_expected&action=edit) |\n| [ranges::single\\_viewviews::single](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/ranges/single_view.html \"cpp/ranges/single view\")<br>(C++20) | a [`view`](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/ranges/view.html \"cpp/ranges/view\") that contains a single element of a specified value<br>(class template)(customization point object)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/ranges/dsc_single_view&action=edit) |\n| [ranges::empty\\_viewviews::empty](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/ranges/empty_view.html \"cpp/ranges/empty view\")<br>(C++20) | an empty [`view`](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/ranges/view.html \"cpp/ranges/view\") with no elements<br>(class template)(variable template)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/ranges/dsc_empty_view&action=edit) |\n\nRetrieved from \" [https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/utility/optional&oldid=180937](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/utility/optional&oldid=180937)\"\n\n##### Navigation\n\n- [Support us](http://www.cppreference.com/support)\n- [Recent changes](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Special:RecentChanges \"A list of recent changes in the wiki [r]\")\n- [FAQ](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Cppreference%253AAbout.html)\n- [Offline version](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Cppreference%253AArchives.html)\n\n##### Toolbox\n\n- [What links here](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Special:WhatLinksHere/cpp/utility/optional \"A list of all wiki pages that link here [j]\")\n- [Related changes](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Special:RecentChangesLinked/cpp/utility/optional \"Recent changes in pages linked from this page [k]\")\n- [Upload file](http://upload.cppreference.com/w/Special:Upload \"Upload files [u]\")\n- [Special pages](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Special:SpecialPages \"A list of all special pages [q]\")\n- [Printable version](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/utility/optional&printable=yes \"Printable version of this page [p]\")\n- [Permanent link](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/utility/optional&oldid=180937 \"Permanent link to this revision of the page\")\n- [Page information](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/utility/optional&action=info)\n\n- In other languages\n\n- [Espa\u00f1ol](http://es.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional \"cpp/utility/optional\")\n- [\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e](http://ja.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional \"cpp/utility/optional\")\n- [\u0420\u0443\u0441\u0441\u043a\u0438\u0439](http://ru.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional \"cpp/utility/optional\")\n- [\u4e2d\u6587](http://zh.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/optional \"cpp/utility/optional\")\n\n- This page was last modified on 19 February 2025, at 01:18.\n\n- [Privacy policy](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Cppreference%253APrivacy_policy.html \"Cppreference:Privacy policy\")\n- [About cppreference.com](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Cppreference%253AAbout.html \"Cppreference:About\")\n- [Disclaimers](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Cppreference%253AGeneral_disclaimer.html \"Cppreference:General disclaimer\")\n\n- [![Powered by MediaWiki](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/skins/common/images/poweredby_mediawiki_88x31.png)](https://www.mediawiki.org/)[![Powered by GeSHi](https://upload.cppreference.com/mwiki/images/2/2b/powered_by_geshi_88x31.png)](http://qbnz.com/highlighter/)[![Hosted by Tiger Technologies](https://upload.cppreference.com/mwiki/images/9/94/powered_by_tigertech_88x31.png)](http://www.tigertech.net/referral/cppreference.com)",
